When you use `ubuntu-latest`, `windows-latest`, or `macos-latest`, GitHub automatically provisions a fresh, temporary virtual machine (known as a **GitHub-hosted runner**) to execute your tasks. These servers are managed by GitHub, and they already have common tools installed, though the `open-policy-agent/setup-opa` action ensures the specific OPA CLI version you need is available.

