xtend your existing GitHub Actions workflow.\n\nThe CI portion continues to handle validation, formatting, and testing on every pull request. The new CD portion (`opa-deploy`) will trigger only when code is merged into the `main` or `master` branches, building a production-ready OPA bundle and providing a template for building and pushing a Docker image for your OPA pod.\n\n```diff\n--- /home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml\n+++ /home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml\n@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@\n-name: OPA CI\n+name: OPA CI/CD\n \n on:\n   push:\n@@ -30,3 +30,30 @@\n       - name: Run OPA Tests\n         run: |\n           opa test . -v\n+\n+  opa-deploy:\n+    name: Build and Deploy OPA Bundle\n+    needs: opa-validation\n+    if: github.event_name == 'push' \u0026\u0026 (github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' || github.ref == 'refs/heads/master')\n+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Checkout code\n+        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n+\n+      - name: Setup OPA CLI\n+        uses: open-policy-agent/setup-opa@v2\n+        with:\n+          version: latest\n+\n+      - name: Build Policy Bundle\n+        run: |\n+          # Compiles Rego policies into a production-optimized bundle\n+          opa build . -o bundle.tar.gz\n+\n+      - name: Build Docker Image for OPA Pod\n+        run: |\n+          # Placeholder for building your OPA container image.\n+          # Replace 'my-opa-pod' with your actual image name and registry URL.\n+          echo \"Building Docker image...\"\n+          # docker build -t my-opa-pod:${{ github.sha }} .\n+          # docker push my-opa-pod:${{ github.sha }}\n```\n\n### Key Additions for CI/CD:\n\n1.  **Workflow Name Update**: Renamed to `OPA CI/CD` to reflect the new capabilities.\n2.  **`opa-deploy` Job**: \n    *   **Dependency**: It uses `needs: opa-validation` to ensure that deployments only happen if all tests and syntax checks pass.\n    *   **Conditional Trigger**: It uses `if: github.event_name == 'push' ...` so that deployments are not triggered on Pull Requests, but only when changes are committed/merged to your primary branch.\n3.  **`opa build`**: This step generates a `.tar.gz` bundle, which is the standard way OPA consumes policies in production pods via the Bundle API.\n4.  **Docker Placeholder**: Since you mentioned an \"OPA pod,\" I've added a placeholder step for the `docker build` process. You can uncomment this and add your specific registry (like Google Artifact Registry or Docker Hub) to automate the full pod update.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How can I configure the OPA pod to automatically pull the new policy bundle from a Google Cloud Storage bucket?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How do I add Google Cloud authentication to this GitHub Action to push the Docker image?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"2","promptCitations":[{"startIndex":935,"endIndex":1168,"filepath":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","citationText":"runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Checkout code\n+        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n+\n+      - name: Setup OPA CLI\n+        uses: open-policy-agent/setup-opa@v2\n+        with:\n+          version: latest\n+\n+      - name"}],"ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":null,"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setuptools/__init__.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setuptools/build_meta.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setuptools/_distutils/dist.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-package