ckages/pip/_internal/vcs/git.py","/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/skills/dbt-bigquery/SKILL.md","/home/mdbaddi/.codeoss/data/User/globalStorage/googlecloudtools.datacloud/skill_bases/dbt-bigquery/SKILL.md","/home/mdbaddi/.codeoss/data/User/globalStorage/googlecloudtools.datacloud/skill_bases/gcp-dataflow/SKILL.md"]},"suggestedPrompts":["How do I generate a Personal Access Token on GitHub?","What do I do if git push says 'error: failed to push some refs'?"],"thinkingSummaryMarkdownText":"**Adding Remote Repository**\n\nI'm currently focused on establishing a connection to my GitHub repository. My immediate goal is to execute the necessary Git command to add the remote, which will then allow me to push my code. This is a critical step before I can proceed with sharing my work.\n\n**Configuring Remote Connection**\n\nI'm refining the process of linking my local project to GitHub. My focus is on presenting the precise `git remote add` command, detailing the usual `origin` name and a placeholder for the repository URL. This ensures the foundational step for pushing code is clearly understood.\n\n","id":"5b8b5f24-f9bd-4dfe-bb7e-effbdf544319","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""},"modelDisplayName":"3 Flash Preview","modelID":"chat-gemini-3-0-flash-preview-free-tier","usageMetadata":{"promptTokenCount":50993,"candidatesTokenCount":409,"totalTokenCount":51402}},{"entity":"USER","markdownText":"mdbaddi@cloudshell:~ (tgs-int-odp-dev-001)$ git push -u origin main\r\nerror: src refspec main does not match any\r\nerror: failed to push some refs to 'https://github.com/Manjuanthtek/odp-runtime.git'","chatSectionId":"7","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"yaml","selection":{"start":1216,"end":1216},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip/_internal/vcs/git.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/config/plugins/googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry/telemetry_hook_bundle.js","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/humanfriendly/terminal/html.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/extensions/vertex/README.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datahub/ingestion/source/snowflake/snowflake_v2.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip/_internal/vcs/git.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/extensions/vertex/README.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.codeoss/data/User/globalStorage/googlecloudtools.datacloud/skill_bases/gcp-composer-troubleshooting/SKILL.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/skills/gcp-composer-troubleshooting/SKILL.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.codeoss/data/User/globalStorage/googlecloudtools.datacloud/skill_bases/dbt-bigquery/SKILL.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"}],"rules":null,"editableRegion":null,"recentUserActions":null,"chatSectionId":"7"},"id":"6a88b097-83e4-43a5-86b0-bd4e068682fa","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""}},{"traceId":"e114a7ad16c75d36","entity":"SYSTEM","markdownText":"The error `error: src refspec main does not match any` typically occurs because Git cannot find a local branch named `main` to push. This happens for one of two reasons:\n\n1.  **The local branch is named `master`**: Older versions of Git initialize the default branch as `master` instead of `main`.\n2.  **No commits exist yet**: Git does not actually \"create\" the branch until you have made at least one commit.\n\nHere are the steps to fix this in your Cloud Shell:\n\n### 1. Check your local branch name\nRun the following command to see what your current branch is called:\n```bash\ngit branch\n```\n*   If it says `* master`, you have a branch named `master`.\n*   If it returns nothing, you haven't committed anything yet.\n\n### 2. If you haven't committed yet\nGit cannot push an empty repository. You must add your files and create the first commit:\n```bash\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit: Add OPA CI/CD workflow\"\n```\n\n### 3. Rename `master` to `main` (Recommended)\nSince your GitHub Actions workflow in `/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml` is configured to look for `main`, it is best to rename your local branch to match:\n```bash\n# Rename the current branch to main\ngit branch -m master main\n\n# Now try pushing again\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n### 4. Alternative: Push `master` directly\nIf you prefer to keep the name `master`, just push that name instead. However, remember to ensure your GitHub repository's default branch settings match:\n```bash\ngit push -u origin master\n```\n\n**Note on Authentication:**\nWhen prompted for a password, remember to use your **GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)**, as GitHub no longer accepts account passwords for command-line Git operations.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How do I create a GitHub Personal Access Token for Cloud Shell?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How can I check if my files were actually added to the commit?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"7","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"yaml","selection":{"start":1216,"end":1216},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remot