y commits are properly synchronized.\n\n**Resolving Branch Push**\n\nMy previous push to `master` failed because it doesn't exist locally. I've identified that my current branch is `test-opa-ci` and need to push that to synchronize my work. I'll then consider merging into `main` to trigger the CI/CD workflow as intended.\n\n**Clarifying Push Operations**\n\nI've realized the `master` push failure stemmed from its absence locally. My focus is now on pushing the current `test-opa-ci` branch to origin. I'll then address renaming to `main` for the CI/CD workflow, ensuring proper synchronization.\n\n**Pushing Current Branch**\n\nI've re-examined the context and realized my previous attempts to push `master` were misguided since it doesn't exist locally. My current focus is pushing the `test-opa-ci` branch to origin using `git push -u origin test-opa-ci`. This should synchronize my work and allow for a Pull Request.\n\n**Pushing Latest Commit**\n\nI'm now focused on pushing my latest commit from the `test-opa-ci` branch to the origin. This action is intended to trigger the CI/CD workflow, which is configured in the GitHub Actions YAML file for the `main` or `master` branches. Following this, I'll initiate a Pull Request on GitHub.\n\n","id":"91a5f105-e08f-4819-97aa-cfeb7888611a","agentMetadata":{"coderAgent":{"kind":""},"model":""},"modelDisplayName":"3 Flash Preview","modelID":"chat-gemini-3-0-flash-preview-free-tier","usageMetadata":{"promptTokenCount":37480,"candidatesTokenCount":497,"totalTokenCount":37977}},{"entity":"USER","markdownText":"why i am not able to create the Pull request using https://github.com/Manjuanthtek/odp-runtime/pull/new/test-opa-ci?","chatSectionId":"9","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"yaml","selection":{"start":1216,"end":1216},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN","isUntitled":false},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/s