ME\u003e` with the name you just created on GitHub:\n\n```bash\n# Add the remote named 'origin'\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/Manjuanthtek/\u003cREPO_NAME\u003e.git\n\n# Verify that it was added correctly\ngit remote -v\n```\n\n### 3. Push your Code\nNow you can push your local changes to GitHub. Note that modern GitHub repositories usually use `main` as the default branch, but older local setups might use `master`.\n\n```bash\n# Check your current branch name\ngit branch\n\n# Push the code (replace 'main' with your branch name if it is different)\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n**Note on Authentication:**\nWhen you push, Git will ask for your username and password. For the password, you must use a **Personal Access Token (PAT)** rather than your actual GitHub password. You can generate one in your GitHub settings under **Developer Settings \u003e Personal access tokens**.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How do I generate a Personal Access Token on GitHub?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]What do I do if git push says 'error: failed to push some refs'?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"6","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"yaml","selection":{"start":1216,"end":1216},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip/_internal/vcs/git.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.codeoss/data/User/globalStorage/googlecloudtools.datacloud/skill_bases/gcp-composer-troubleshooting/SKILL.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/skills/gcp-composer-troubleshooting/SKILL.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datahub/ingestion/source/looker/loo