ent":{"kind":""},"model":""}},{"traceId":"bf79c28efa68ee18","entity":"SYSTEM","markdownText":"The reason you are likely unable to create the Pull Request using that link is that your branch **`test-opa-ci` has not been successfully pushed to GitHub yet**.\n\nIn your previous terminal logs, I noticed that when you ran `git push -u origin test-opa-ci`, the command was interrupted (indicated by the `^C`). Additionally, when you tried to push `master`, it failed because that branch doesn't exist locally. GitHub cannot create a Pull Request for a branch it doesn't know about.\n\nTo fix this and enable the Pull Request creation, follow these steps in your Cloud Shell:\n\n### 1. Push the branch to GitHub\nRun the command again and let it complete. When prompted for a password, use your **GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)**:\n\n```bash\ngit push -u origin test-opa-ci\n```\n\n### 2. Verify the push\nAfter the command finishes, you should see output similar to:\n` * [new branch]      test-opa-ci -\u003e test-opa-ci`\n\n### 3. Create the Pull Request\nOnce the branch is on GitHub, you have three ways to create the PR:\n1.  **Direct Link**: Your link `https://github.com/Manjuanthtek/odp-runtime/pull/new/test-opa-ci` will now work perfectly.\n2.  **Repo Homepage**: If you visit `https://github.com/Manjuanthtek/odp-runtime`, you will see a yellow bar at the top saying *\"test-opa-ci had recent pushes\"* with a **Compare \u0026 pull request** button.\n3.  **Command Line**: The output of the `git push` command usually provides a clickable URL specifically for creating the PR.\n\n### Troubleshooting\n*   **Authentication**: If it asks for a password and fails, remember that GitHub **does not accept your account password** for Git operations. You must generate a Personal Access Token (Classic) in your GitHub Settings.\n*   **No Changes**: If GitHub says \"There isn’t anything to compare,\" it means your `test-opa-ci` branch is identical to your `main` branch. Ensure you have committed your changes to the `.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml` file locally first using `git add .` and `git commit -m \"add ci/cd\"`.\n\n\u003c!--\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]How do I generate a GitHub Personal Access Token for the command line?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n[PROMPT_SUGGESTION]What should I do if my GitHub Actions workflow doesn't start after I create the Pull Request?[/PROMPT_SUGGESTION]\n--\u003e","chatSectionId":"9","ideContext":{"currentFile":{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.github/workflows/opa-ci.yml","language":"yaml","selection":{"start":1216,"end":1216},"includedReason":"CURRENTLY_OPEN"},"remoteContexts":null,"remoteRepositories":[],"otherFiles":[{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/setuptools/_distutils/tests/test_config_cmd.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip/_vendor/requests/status_codes.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datahub/utilities/partition_executor.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/docker/models/networks.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datahub/utilities/file_backed_collections.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip/_internal/vcs/git.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.gemini/extensions/vertex/README.md","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED_FILE"},{"path":"/home/mdbaddi/.local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/datahub/configuration/git.py","language":"","selection":{"start":0,"end":0},"includedReason":"RELATED